/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 104 0 R
/T (Existing vehicle communication systems mainly rely on RF technologies, which often face issues such as spectrum congestion, electromagnetic interference, and security risks. Additionally, many systems do not effectively integrate accident detection and vehicle monitoring within a single platform. There is also a growing need for intelligent communication systems in dark factory environments, where automated robots and vehicles must operate and communicate efficiently with minimal human intervention. )
/E (Existing vehicle communication systems mainly rely on RF technologies, which often face issues such as spectrum congestion, electromagnetic interference, and security risks. Additionally, many systems do not effectively integrate accident detection and vehicle monitoring within a single platform. There is also a growing need for intelligent communication systems in dark factory environments, where automated robots and vehicles must operate and communicate efficiently with minimal human intervention. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
