140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (The EVBHARAT system proposes a smart vehicle prototype that integrates Vehicle-to-Vehicle \(V2V\) communication using Visible Light Communication \(VLC\) along with multiple sensors for monitoring and safety. The system uses an ESP32 microcontroller to process data from different sensors and control the overall operation. LEDs act as transmitters and a photodiode receives the VLC signals for secure communication between vehicles. An ultrasonic sensor is used to measure the distance between the bot and obstacles to ensure safe movement in a dark factory environment. Additionally, an MPU6050 accelerometer and vibration sensor help detect sudden impacts or accidents, while a temperature sensor and voltage monitoring system track battery condition. Together, these sensors enable safe navigation, accident detection, vehicle communication, and efficient automation. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
